{"type":"new-conversation","conversation":{"id":1000002,"start_time":"2026-01-01T11:00:00.000Z","end_time":null,"conversation_uuid":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000000b","device_type":"unknown","device_id":null,"summary":null,"short_summary":null,"state":"CAPTURING","primary_location":null,"template":null,"city":null,"business":null,"bookmarked":false}}
{"type":"new-utterance","conversation_uuid":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000000b","utterance":{"id":4100001,"sample_id":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000a1","start":10.0,"end":24.5,"text":"An arch turns the weight of the bridge into compression, which stone and brick handle well, so the load travels down the curve to the supports at each end.","spoken_at":"2026-01-01T11:00:10.000Z"}}
{"type":"new-utterance","conversation_uuid":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000000b","utterance":{"id":4100002,"sample_id":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000a2","start":24.5,"end":40.0,"text":"The supports at each end are called abutments, and they have to push back against the sideways thrust, otherwise the arch would spread apart and collapse.","spoken_at":"2026-01-01T11:00:25.000Z"}}
{"type":"new-utterance","conversation_uuid":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000000b","utterance":{"id":4100003,"sample_id":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000a3","start":90.0,"end":118.0,"text":"The keystone is the wedge shaped block at the top, and once it is in place the two halves lock together so that the whole arch holds itself up without scaffolding.","spoken_at":"2026-01-01T11:01:30.000Z"}}
{"type":"new-utterance","conversation_uuid":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000000b","utterance":{"id":4100004,"sample_id":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000a4","start":150.0,"end":158.0,"text":"So the main idea is that a curve can carry a load that a flat span could not.","spoken_at":"2026-01-01T11:02:30.000Z"}}
